{\b\fs28\cf1 .RAV IDE 2.4}\par
{\cf2 Simulation suite & IDE for Tulpa \endash  formerly HermiSim}\par\par
{\b What gets installed}\par
\bullet  {\b .RAV IDE} \endash  editor with Tulpa language server, run configurations, static proofs of contracts, native and firmware builds (RP2040, ESP32) for any program, including the whole language on the Tulpa VM for firmware, one-step deploy, a Tulpa Link network view and serial bridge, telemetry plots, VCD waveform viewer, state-machine diagrams, BOM/netlist viewer.\par
\bullet  {\b MuJoCo co-simulator} \endash  Tulpa programs drive physics through {\f1 cosim::connect()}; headless runs via {\f1 ravide-cli}.\par
\bullet  {\b Tulpa toolchain} \endash  {\f1 tulpa} interpreter, bytecode VM, LLVM {\f1 build} (executables and microcontroller firmware), the Tulpa VM for firmware, {\f1 new}, {\f1 verify}, {\f1 lsp}, plus the {\f1 std/} libraries: rtl, eda, rl, lipm, topics, frame, driver and drivers (MPU-6050, PCA9685, MCP3008), plan, link, world, emu, verify, and native {\f1 nn::}, {\f1 pack::}, {\f1 json::}, {\f1 cosim::}.\par
\bullet  {\b Licence} \endash  Business Source License 1.1: free for development, evaluation, education and research; commercial production use is licensed by HermiTech LLC.\par
\bullet  {\b Morty} \endash  bipedal humanoid sample: capture-point balance, physics-informed COM model, PPO residual policy, FPGA torque governor (RTL + behavioural), mainboard as code.\par\par
{\b Where things go}\par
Program files: the folder you choose next.  Your projects: {\f1 Documents\\RAV IDE} (created on first launch; an existing {\f1 Documents\\HermiSim} is kept).  Logs: {\f1 %LOCALAPPDATA%\\RAV IDE}.\par\par
{\b Requirements}\par
Windows 10 1809 or later, 64-bit. OpenGL 3.3 capable graphics for the 3-D viewport.\par
